      "prompt": "Explain, with a diagram described in words, why (a + b)² is not equal to a² + b².",
      "modelAnswer": "Draw a square with side a + b. Split each side into a and b. The square splits into four parts: an a × a square (a²), a b × b square (b²), and two a × b rectangles (2ab). So (a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b². Writing a² + b² leaves out the two rectangles. For example, (3 + 4)² = 49, but 3² + 4² = 25.",
